    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Johnson returns five weeks after sertraline was increased to 100 mg. He is writing most mornings again and dines with friends several times a week. He wakes less often in dread. He has mild night sweats and no other side effects. He has had six of eight sessions of behavioral therapy for tics and uses the competing response for the head-shaking tic in company; the clucking sounds are less frequent. There was no check two weeks after the dose increase. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>100 mg daily for five weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 10</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Writing most mornings; seeing friends</td></tr><tr><td>Tic therapy</td><td>Six of eight sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Mild night sweats</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

